// ⚠ **EDITING THIS FILE MOVES A LINE NUMBER THE EXPECTATION PINS.** The report names the
// ASSERTION'S OWN line — `Expect`'s `file`/`line` default to `__file__`/`__line__`, which expand at
// the CALL SITE — so that number is part of the contract and not incidental. Insert a line above one
// and `expected.txt` is owed a regeneration; the gate's report will say which line differs.
// The FAILING report: one test green, one red, and the `expected:`/`received:` detail block under
// it. The same subject as `all-pass`, so the two fixtures differ only in whether the expectation
// written against it is right — which is what makes their two reports comparable.
typealias Cents = int(0 to i64.max)

function totalCost(unitPrice Cents, quantity Cents) returns Cents
	let gross = unitPrice * quantity
	if quantity < 10 'noDiscount'
		return gross
	end 'noDiscount'

	return gross - gross / 10
end 'totalCost'

test 'a small order pays full price'
	try Expect.equal(totalCost(250, quantity: 4), expected: 1000)
end 'a small order pays full price'

// Deliberately wrong — it forgot the discount. This is the fixture's whole subject.
test 'ten items take the bulk discount'
	try Expect.equal(totalCost(250, quantity: 10), expected: 2500)
end 'ten items take the bulk discount'
